<title>SOUTH KOREA: Bank of Korea steps in, buying dollars at 891.10.</title>
<headline>Bank of Korea steps in, buying dollars at 891.10.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1997-06-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>The central Bank of Korea intervened in the domestic inter-bank foreign exchange market in Tuesday's morning trading, buying dollars at 891.10, dealers said.  </p>
<p>The won fell to 891.40 after the intervention, dealers said.</p>
<p>After opening at 891.50, the won rose to 891.00.</p>
<p>Dealers said the Bank of Korea bought dollars to soak up abundant dollar positions in the market.</p>
<p>The central bank does not confirm its interventions.</p>
<p>-- Seoul Newsroom (822) 727 5647</p>
</text>
